# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/analytics` package (97 dependencies added)
- **Modified**: `frontend/package.json` - Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies
- **Modified**: `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **Modified**: `frontend/src/App.jsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main app container
  - Component placed inside the root div element to track all page views and interactions

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Configuration
This is a React + Vite project, so I used the React-specific import path:
```javascript
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';
```

### Component Placement
The `<Analytics />` component was added to the root App component, just before the closing `</div>` tag. This ensures:
- Analytics tracks all user interactions across both tabs (Peta hotspot and Verifikasi citra)
- The component is rendered once and persists throughout the application lifecycle
- Minimal impact on existing component structure

### Verification Steps Completed
1. ✅ Package installation successful (npm install completed without errors)
2. ✅ Build verification passed (vite build completed successfully in 999ms)
3. ✅ Linter check passed (oxlint found 0 errors, only 1 pre-existing warning unrelated to changes)
4. ✅ No breaking changes introduced
5. ✅ Lock file properly updated

## Next Steps for Deployment
1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics sidebar → Enable button)
3. After deployment, verify analytics are working by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
4. Monitor the analytics dashboard in Vercel to see visitor data

## Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- No additional configuration is needed for basic page view tracking
- Custom events and advanced features can be added later if needed (available on Pro/Enterprise plans)
- The implementation preserves all existing functionality and code structure
